    "node-12diii6": {
      "supported": false,
      "issue": "The claim that 'Daily work briefing contained no valve-by-valve content' is supported by the text of the attendance sheet excerpt which states: 'Its topic line reads “1SC dryer work and RHOB service coordination.” It contains no valve-by-valve content.' However, this supports only what was written on the sheet. The claim implies a causal link to safety (i.e., that missing detail caused risk). Without evidence of an applicable requirement for such detail in briefings or proof that omission led directly to error, treating it as fully supported risks conflating observation with causation.",
      "evidenceNeeded": "Evidence establishing whether the absence of valve-by-valve content violated a specific procedure at this work stage (preparation) and how that gap contributed to the event.","question":"Does WO-527 or site policy require valve-by-valve briefing for 1SC dryer maintenance, and was such detail omitted in violation?"
    },
    "node-1ka5agi": {
      "supported": false,
      "issue": "The claim 'No evidence crew received recent change briefing or saw specific configuration drawing used' is marked unknown. The excerpt states: 'Training extract does not state which configuration drawing the crew saw; no interview concerning fatigue... included.' This correctly reflects absence of direct evidence but treats it as a condition rather than an inference requiring validation against procedural expectations.",
      "evidenceNeeded": "A record showing whether change briefings were required for this work and if any briefing occurred, or confirmation that none was given.","question":"Was there a documented requirement to receive a recent configuration drawing review before starting boundary preparation on WO-527?"
    },
